From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Subject: [PATCH] media/gpu/v4l2: derive the planes of single-buffer P010

V4L2FormatToVideoFrameLayout() derives the colour planes that a V4L2
buffer does not describe only for NV12, YUV420 and YVU420. A stateless
decoder that returns 10-bit pictures as single-buffer V4L2_PIX_FMT_P010
(the V4L2 API has no multi-buffer P010) therefore fails with "Cannot
derive stride for each plane for pixel format P010": no frame can be
created from the CAPTURE buffers, and 10-bit VP9, AV1 and HEVC video
stalls without falling back to software decode.

P010 has the plane geometry of NV12 with 16-bit samples: the
interleaved CbCr plane uses the Y stride and half the Y height. Derive
it like NV12.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
--- a/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_utils.cc
+++ b/media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_utils.cc
@@ -272,7 +272,8 @@
   }
   // For the case that #color planes > #buffers, it fills stride of color
   // plane which does not map to buffer.
-  // Right now only some pixel formats are supported: NV12, YUV420, YVU420.
+  // Right now only some pixel formats are supported: NV12, P010, YUV420,
+  // YVU420.
   if (num_color_planes > num_buffers) {
     const int32_t y_stride = UNSAFE_TODO(planes[0]).stride;
     // Note that y_stride is from v4l2 bytesperline and its type is uint32_t.
@@ -280,6 +281,10 @@
     const size_t y_stride_abs = static_cast<size_t>(y_stride);
     switch (pix_fmt) {
       case V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12:
+      // P010 has the plane geometry of NV12 with two bytes per sample: the
+      // interleaved UV plane shares the Y stride (bytesperline already counts
+      // the 16-bit samples) and is half the height of the Y plane.
+      case V4L2_PIX_FMT_P010:
         // The stride of UV is the same as Y in NV12.
         // The height is half of Y plane.
         planes.emplace_back(y_stride, y_stride_abs * pix_mp.height,
